      "artist": "Marc Merlin",
      "description": "Vertical panorama showing Bank of America Plaza—Atlanta’s tallest skyscraper at 1,023 ft (312 m)—rising behind the Fox Theatre on Peachtree Street in Midtown. Completed in 1992 and designed by Kevin Roche John Dinkeloo and Associates, the postmodern tower contrasts with the Fox Theatre’s 1929 Moorish Revival design, a National Historic Landmark and one of Atlanta’s most celebrated architectural treasures. The composition highlights two icons of different eras, representing over six decades of the city’s architectural evolution.",
